{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1458068-questions-about-spirit-combat-stare-down","id":1458068,"title":"Questions about spirit combat & stare down","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-30T11:01:36-07:00","id":1458068,"title":"Questions about spirit combat & stare down","content":"Gonna keep this one quick:<ul><li>Is there a way for spirits/banes to take multiple actions during a round?</li> <li>Do you have all spirits inflict aggravated damage when striking with their claws/talons/what have you?</li> </ul>Staredown: I've now been in two situations where both garou involved reached the same number of needed successes at the same time. What happens then?<br /> <br /> Thanks!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26645-pwtucker","name":"pwtucker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26645_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-30T13:50:45-07:00","id":1458076,"title":"","content":"1) The rules just say to use Willpower rating in place of actions that would normally use Dexterity of Strength. So if you want to split that dice pool into multiple actions like someone would if they had Dex + Brawl, I would think that is OK. And if you wanted to invent a special Charm that gave them extra actions without penalties, that should be fine too. That way not every spirit could do it, but certain spirits could. Or if you rule that a spirit can spend its Rage to get multiple actions just like a Garou can, I think that can work too although I would be leery of that. A Scrag with 10 Rage (or even 6 if you go with the errata that accompanies every edition - yet the next corebook never revises a Scrag's Rage) could quickly become too powerful under that rule. <br /> <br /> I think in general a spirit should be able to do it by some means, although you may want to discuss specifics with your game group.<br /> <br /> 2) I only have &quot;appropriate&quot; spirits be able to inflict aggravated damage with their claw/talon attacks. It depends on how deadly you want the spirit to be. For example, on one side of the spectrum is a deer spirit who might attack in the form of its hooves or antlers. I wouldn't give that spirit aggravated damage. I'd give them whatever damage type their animal or whatever normally has. On the other side would be a Psychomachiae, a powerful Bane associated with serial killers. I would give that spirit aggravated damage. Everything in between really depends on how you view the spirits. Scrags, for example, would also seem to be appropriate for aggravated damage. But they are also called foot soldiers of the Wyrm and many games use them as disposable cannon fodder. If you throw masses of Scrags at the PCs, would it be too much if they always did aggravated damage? It might be. But what if you use Scrags sparingly? In that case, giving them aggravated damage might not be unbalancing and provide them with the right amount of menace. So what about normal predator spirits like scorpions, venomous snakes, wolf spirits, eagle spirits, etc.? I would keep most of these at doing lethal damage although there is an argument that any poisonous animal (like a scorpion or viper) should be able do aggravated damage (does that mean a Garou who has the Resist Toxin Gift should reduce that agg to lethal damage? maybe.). But even if rule that Gaffling spirits of this type only do lethal, I might still have a more powerful Jaggling spirit be able to do aggravated in order to showcase the difference in spirit types and their increased power.<br /> <br /> Your sweet spot might be different than mine, but I'm sure you'll find a comfort zone in the kind of chronicle you run.<br /> <br /> 3) I don't think there are rules on tiebreaking. I think there's several ways you could determine a tie-breaker. Decide on whatever tie-breaker makes best sense to you. Discuss it with your group to get buy-in, as you'll need to apply it consistently. One possibility is to rule that higher Rank wins ties. That won't prevent all issues, but it allows quick resolution and helps reinforce hierarchy. Something similar is to rule that higher Willpower stat (or Wits), although again its possible for characters to have equal Willpower. Another possibility is that you use the rules for losers in Facedowns - both characters now needs to decide if they want to roll Willpower to keep going each additional round, and if so the rolls continue until one side gets more successes and wins. Or you may want to have a combination of factors. Or something else strikes you as making sense. Personally, I would probably make both characters spend Willpower to continue and have them keeping rolling as that's already in the rules for what the loser can do. But you and your group might have a different favorite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-30T16:19:53-07:00","id":1458086,"title":"","content":"1) I'd rather remove the ability of Garou to use Rage for extra actions, or limit them like Vampire Dark Age 20th Anniversary Edition did with Celerity. Extra Actions in every game system I played were broken, in my experience. Last week I got into storytelling WtA again, and went with a bonus of half the permanent Rage as Bonus dice to an action, for every point of Rage spend. Also changed the rules for multiple actions, so they use the largest dice pool minus the total number of actions to be divided, so the bonus dice from spend Rage actually get used. Dicepools of actions that aren't suitable for Rage bonuses in my opinion, however, can't be larger in a multiple action scenario than the originally are. But besides that, I agree with Black Fox on the ability to split dice pools of sprits and possibly the need to invent a &quot;multiple actions&quot; Charm.<br /> <br /> 2) + 3) I also agree with Black Fox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-31T01:22:03-07:00","id":1458112,"title":"","content":"I would also rather get rid of extra actions for Rage, but actually not for spirits necessarily.<br /> <br /> Action economy in combat is the single most important factor for balance in any system, but it is also regularly the downfall of &quot;bosses&quot;, enemies that should be able to be a threat for an entire group. And some spirits are clearly in this area, they should by all means have access to extra actions of some kind to be able to deal with an entire Pack.<br /> <br /> One interesting option in this regard may be to have the spirit have access to special reactions, so instead of a ton of actions in its turn, it is able to act several times during combat as it responds to each assailant. D&amp;D 5e have two interesting mechanics that would fit to be adapted as Charms for such spirits, Lair Actions and Legendary Actions.<br /> <br /> That aside, also agree with Black Fox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}